        "y2": 665.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.8644986152648926,
      "reading_order": 4,
      "text": "5. $Z = \\frac{29392}{1837} = 16$\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260317_fac1ab83-81e6-422f-84cf-3b23b86ae39a_1_block_004",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 236.0,
        "y1": 695.0,
        "x2": 1170.0,
        "y2": 1041.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9316682815551758,
      "reading_order": 5,
      "text": "6. A dipositively charged helium ion is $\\alpha$ particle.\nA helium atom has 2 electrons, 2 protons, and\n2 neutrons. When 2 electrons are removed, it is\nleft with 2 protons and 2 neutrons that means 4\nfundamental particles.\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260317_fac1ab83-81e6-422f-84cf-3b23b86ae39a_1_block_005",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 234.0,
        "y1": 1070.0,
        "x2": 1167.0,
        "y2": 1252.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9135231375694275,
      "reading_order": 6,
      "text": "7. The presence of nucleus in an atom was first\nestablished by Rutherford.\nHence, the correct option is (a)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260317_fac1ab83-81e6-422f-84cf-3b23b86ae39a_1_block_006",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 234.0,
        "y1": 1273.0,
        "x2": 1169.0,
        "y2": 1508.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9256399273872375,
      "reading_order": 7,
      "text": "8. Platinum is also highly malleable and has high\nnuclear charge. So, it can replace gold foil in\n$\\alpha$-ray scattering experiment.\nHence, the correct option is (c)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260317_fac1ab83-81e6-422f-84cf-3b23b86ae39a_1_block_007",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 232.0,
        "y1": 1533.0,
        "x2": 1171.0,
        "y2": 1768.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.922633945941925,
      "reading_order": 8,
      "text": "9. An atom with $Z = 7$ and $Z = 15$ has electronic\nconfigurations 2, 5 and 2, 8, 5. These two can\nform trinegative ions.\n\nHence, the correct option is (d)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260317_fac1ab83-81e6-422f-84cf-3b23b86ae39a_1_block_008",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 216.0,
        "y1": 1790.0,
        "x2": 1170.0,
        "y2": 1971.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9035106897354126,
      "reading_order": 9,
      "text": "10. Noble gases or inert gases have 8 valence\nelectrons.\n\nHence, the correct option is (c)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260317_fac1ab83-81e6-422f-84cf-3b23b86ae39a_1_block_009",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1265.0,
        "y1": 291.0,
        "x2": 2218.0,
        "y2": 527.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.931069016456604,
      "reading_order": 10,
      "text": "11. The electronic configuration of element X is 2,\n8, 10, and 2. The atomic number of the element\nis 22.\n\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260317_fac1ab83-81e6-422f-84cf-3b23b86ae39a_1_block_010",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1264.0,
        "y1": 557.0,
        "x2": 2221.0,
        "y2": 794.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9133616089820862,
      "reading_order": 11,
      "text": "12. Electron releases energy when it moves from M\nshell to L shell, since M shell has greater energy\nthan L shell.\n\nHence, the correct option is (a)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260317_fac1ab83-81e6-422f-84cf-3b23b86ae39a_1_block_011",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1264.0,
        "y1": 829.0,
        "x2": 2218.0,
        "y2": 1191.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9281108975410461,
      "reading_order": 12,
      "text": "13. $\\alpha$-ray scattering experiment was conducted\nto prove the validity of Thomson’s model. All\nthe $\\alpha$-particles were expected to pass straight\nthrough the gold foil since the positively\ncharged mass is uniformly distributed.\nHence, the correct option is (d)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260317_fac1ab83-81e6-422f-84cf-3b23b86ae39a_1_block_012",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1262.0,
        "y1": 1221.0,
        "x2": 2211.0,
        "y2": 1556.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.8283984065055847,
      "reading_order": 13,
      "text": "14. Electronic arrangement of an element having\natomic number 24 $\\rightarrow$ 2, 8, 13, 1\nK L M N\nSo, the antepenultimate shell has 8 electrons.\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260317_fac1ab83-81e6-422f-84cf-3b23b86ae39a_1_block_013",
